 "notes": "Electrostatic linear ion trap for CDMS, r-z symmetry, built from J. A. Hogan & M. F. Jarrold, J. Am. Soc. Mass Spectrom. 29, 2086-2095 (2018), DOI 10.1007/s13361-018-2007-x (cylindrical trap): mirror electrodes l=4.57 mm, ID=13.97 mm, spacing delta=0.127 mm; grounded shields 3.81 mm thick with EXACT beveled bore 13.97 -> 3.3 mm (polygon); field-free 50.8 mm holding the 50.04 x 6.35 mm-ID charge-detection tube; endcap aperture r=1.5 mm. VOLTAGES ARE BRIAN'S SLIDE (2026-08-12), TRAPPED STATE: E1 133.4, E2 140.1, E3+endcaps 217.1 V, shields/tube 0 V, both mirrors symmetric. TRANSMISSION ('red') state, entrance mirror only: E3_L+endcap_L -> 0.0 V, E2_L -> 105.0 V (gate open; back mirror already trapping) \u2014 encode with two table-waveform step groups when gating is simulated, exactly as the oa-TOF time-lag example does. Paper's own tune for reference: E1 135, E2 95/125, E3 0/190 V at 130 eV/z. MODELING ASSUMPTIONS (not in the paper): endcap = aperture plate 1.52 mm thick at the E3 potential (slide shows an L-shaped endcap); electrode outer radius 12.0 mm; detector tube wall 0.8 mm; upstream segmented quadrupole/hexapole beamline NOT modeled \u2014 the source stands in for it: ions born on axis at trap center, 130.0 eV/z along +x (the paper's own simulation initial condition). Cell 0.0635 mm/gu = 2 cells per delta gap. TUNED 2026-08-12 (Fig 3c reproduction, within 's +-10 V wiggle around the slide): E1 133.4 -> 124.4, E2 140.1 -> 148.1, E3+endcaps 217.1 unchanged. Axial energy-isochronism slope at 130 eV/z, m/z 50000 (quadrature on the solved axis potential, validated by flight): slide tune +0.8094 %f/%E -> tuned -0.0078 %f/%E (paper cylindrical -0.0899, conical -0.903). f(130 eV) = 4.099 kHz, period 244 us -- the long period is PHYSICAL for 50 kDa at 130 eV/z (field-free transit alone is 143 us/round trip); it is why short flights show few oscillations. Radial stability at the tuned point NOT yet characterized (Fig 2 stability map is the natural next study). COLLISIONS OFF (2026-08-12): the first cut authored collisions:{model:'none'}, which set the MODEL string while `enabled` defaulted TRUE at 1 Torr N2 -- the trap was flying in a Torr of gas, which read as mysterious axial drag + radial diffusion to the tube wall. Paper operating pressure is 2e-9 Torr; vacuum (enabled:false) is the correct model.",
